 ## Overview
-SpLap is a proxy-free deformation framework for Gaussian Splatting that enables high-quality, large-scale geometric editing without relying on external meshes or cages. It constructs a surface-aware splat graph based on kernel intersections to estimate local geometry, allowing Laplacian-based deformation techniques to be applied directly to the Gaussian primitives. Unlike proxy-based methods such as [Gaussian Frosting](15863-gaussian-frosting.md) or [SuGaR](15863-gaussian-frosting.md), which depend on explicit geometric templates, SpLap avoids proxy defects and mesh generation overhead. Unlike [LBO-GS](15421-scene-representation-and-geometry-constraints.md), which uses Mahalanobis distance and is sensitive to anisotropic primitives, SpLap uses intersection-based connectivity for robust surface estimation.
+SpLap is a proxy-free deformation framework for Gaussian Splatting that enables high-quality, large-scale geometric editing without relying on external meshes or cages [S1]. It constructs a surface-aware splat graph based on kernel intersections to estimate local geometry, allowing Laplacian-based deformation techniques to be applied directly to the Gaussian primitives [S1]. Unlike proxy-based methods such as [Gaussian Frosting](15863-gaussian-frosting.md) or [SuGaR](15863-gaussian-frosting.md), which depend on explicit geometric templates, SpLap avoids proxy defects and mesh generation overhead [S1]. Unlike [LBO-GS](15421-scene-representation-and-geometry-constraints.md), which uses Mahalanobis distance and is sensitive to anisotropic primitives, SpLap uses intersection-based connectivity for robust surface estimation [S1].
 
